## Customizing Charts

Charts can be customized with [Themes](./themes/), [Layouts](./layout/), and [Backgrounds](./background/).

### Layout

The chart will [auto-size](./layout/#chart-size) by default, taking the size of the container element and auto-sizing the chart dynamically.

Use the `width` and/or `height` options if a fixed size is required:

```js
{
    width: 800,
    height: 600,
}
```

### Background

Use `background.fill` to set the [Background](./background/) of the chart to any CSS Color:

```js
background: {
    fill: 'transparent', // or RGB, HEX, HSL, HWB, or named color
},
```

### Themes

AG Charts comes with 5 [Themes](./themes/), each available in light or dark mode.

Use the `theme` property to set the theme:

```js
{
    theme: 'ag-default', // or 'ag-sheets', 'ag-polychrome', 'ag-material', 'ag-vivid'
}
```

Themes can also be customised with the [Theming API](/charts/themes-api/).

Use `params` to set styles across the whole chart, `overrides` to merge over the defaults within the base theme, and `palette` to define the colour palette:

```js
const customTheme: AgChartTheme = {
    palette: {
        fills: ['#5C2983', '#0076C5', '#21B372', '#FDDE02', '#F76700', '#D30018'],
        strokes: ['#881008'],
    },
    params: {
        fontFamily: 'Georgia, serif',
        fontSize: 16,
    },
    overrides: {
        common: {
            title: {
                fontSize: 24,
            },
        },
        bar: {
            series: {
                label: {
                    enabled: true,
                    color: 'white',
                },
            },
        },
    }
};
```

### Example

This example demonstrates a fixed-size chart with a custom theme and background color:

